   "created_utc": "2017-06-08T01:36:27Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<i>PLEASE</i> just use the modern language features such as <code>std::unique_ptr</code> or <code>std::shared_ptr</code> if you can.  I&#39;m very suspicious of this variable you&#39;ve declared in your header, too.  Chances are you forgot to declare it as <code>extern</code>, and it might be uninitialized because there are multiple copies of it.  There are other problems with an external global variable too, such as the <a href=\"https://isocpp.org/wiki/faq/ctors#static-init-order\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Static Initialization Order Fiasco</a>"
  },
